  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The corridor – long pass, shot and defence",
  "description": "The same corridors as the drop-pass drill: line A by the net with all the pucks, line B at the other end. A plays a firm pass – directly or off the boards – to B, who carries the puck at speed towards the net and shoots. A joins the back of line B, and B joins line A.\n\nStep two: after the pass, A skates out and sets up before the centre line as a defender. B has to get past A and shoot. Two more lines can use the other corridor at the same time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the ice to the blade, even when it goes off the boards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The receiver takes the puck forward with the first touch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defender: skate backwards between the attacker and the net and force them out towards the boards."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
